XB-Kidux-Ages: 6-14
Description: Kidux learning module: Simulations, PhET's science and maths experiments
 Kidux is a Debian derivative for a child's first computer. This learning
 module is a set of PhET Interactive Simulations, of the University of
 Colorado Boulder: experiments with numbers, forces, light, electricity,
 matter, planets and life, chosen for ages six to fourteen and sorted by
 group and age in a page of Kidux's own, served on this computer and shown
 in Chromium, in the child's language, without the internet. They are the
 versions PhET published under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
 licence; Kidux is not connected with PhET.
 .
 Once it is installed, an adult switches it on for each child on the
 Modules page of the adult panel.
